# The stand-alone replay of the coupled run of Tests/ERFReplay, with
# FILE=<path>/ERFRain/flume_basin and then flume.rain.type = gridded and
# flume.rain.file = <the index> on the command line (the last value of a key
# is the one read). The grid is the one ERF sets in Tests/ERFRain/
# inputs_kessler: 32 x 32 cells of 50 m (ERF's 16 x 16 columns refined by
# erf.flood.grid_ratio = 2), periodic in x and y. The boxes are not ERF's:
# 16 boxes of 8 x 8 cells, 4 per rank on 4 ranks (the coupled run has 4).
# A plotfile every 60 steps; flume.max_dt = 0.25 s is ERF's step, so each run
# takes one FLUME step per ERF step. The index is read step by step
# (flume.rain.interpolation = step, the default).
flume.n_cell        = 32 32
flume.prob_hi       = 1600.0 1600.0
flume.periodic      = 1 1
flume.max_grid_size = 8
flume.plot_file     = flood
flume.plot_int      = 60
flume.max_dt        = 0.25
flume.stop_time     = 30.0
